+### Reusable model plans
+
+Model plans share a bounded, process-local dispatch cache across layers. Its
+key includes the CUDA device, backend/layout, model geometry and dtypes,
+attention features, validation mode, and effective batch/Q/KV bounds. The first
+layer prepares a dispatch record; later compatible layers reuse its policy,
+compiled executables, and workspace layout without constructing another child
+plan. Concurrent misses for the same key have one builder.
+
+Each wrapper still owns its workspace views, scale tensors, variable-window
+buffers, request metadata bindings and captured execution records. Softmax and
+output scale values are bound from the current layer. The shared cache retains
+no tensor storage, and eviction does not invalidate already prepared wrappers
+or CUDA graphs. Each wrapper must be warmed before its own graph capture.
+
+This dispatch cache complements the persistent CuTe kernel cache and device
+occupancy cache adopted from [PR #6529](https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/6529).
+The merged compilation helper supplies source/target-aware disk keys; the new
+dispatch cache avoids repeated per-layer CPU preparation during eager runs.
+Different runtime bounds still form distinct dispatch entries, and each new
+workload requires one resolution in the process. Compiled kernel reuse remains
+independent of dispatch-record eviction.
+
+Wrappers also accept model configuration in the constructor. In this form,
+`get_workspace_size()` queries scratch bytes without allocating execution
+workspace or compiling kernels, and `plan()` can bind the caller's allocation:
+
