+The CUDA FP32 vector `[Hq]` holds sink logits in natural-log score units after
+QK scaling. Each sink adds denominator mass and zero V contribution. Finite
+values and `-inf` are accepted; NaN and positive infinity are rejected when
+validation is enabled. Final normalization merges sink mass stably before
+output rounding, exactly once after any split reduction. LSE includes the
+sink mass. Default plans compile away this feature; values remain runtime
+inputs and may change between completed graph replays.
