+### Final softmax statistics
+
+Plan with `lse_mode="base2"` or `"basee"` and run with `return_lse=True`
+to receive `(output, lse)`. LSE is compact FP32 with the query shape minus
+the last dimension. An optional caller `lse` buffer is written even when
+`return_lse=False`; supplying both outputs supports allocation-free graph
+replay with validation disabled. The default `lse_mode="none"` keeps the
+output-only path. Final stores remove internal FP8 probability amplification;
+intermediate split statistics retain their native reduction convention.
+LSE excludes output scaling. Buffers must not overlap live inputs, each other,
+or workspace.
+
+Scalar FP8 dequantization is caller-composed: for stored Q/K/V with scales
+`s_q`, `s_k`, `s_v`, use effective QK scale `sm_scale * s_q * s_k` and output
+scale `s_v * desired_output_scale`. Context planning calls these `sm_scale`
+and `output_scale`; context run accepts a one-element FP32
+`scale_softmax_log2 = effective_QK_scale * log2(e)` and `output_scale`.
+FMHA/MLA decode call them `bmm1_scale` and `bmm2_scale`. Per-tensor scalar
+scales are not automatically inferred from FP8 storage. Packed NVFP4 block
+scales remain a separate input contract.
+
