+### Runtime split-KV policy
+
+Split counts and maximum counts are private policy state. The hardware ceiling
+defaults to the device's physical SM count (152 on the validation GB300).
+The policy bounds useful work using planned geometry and KV capacity, then
+prepares scratch/reduction capacity in ranges 1, 2–4, 5–8, 9–16, 17–32, 33–64,
+sixteen-split ranges above64 clipped to the hardware ceiling. A range boundary is not an
+architectural limit. No user count/ceiling or count tensor is required.
+
+Requested counts are typed runtime launch operands in producers and reducers.
+Scratch strides and cluster/barrier participation retain prepared capacity;
+inactive slots/ranks contribute neutral state and preserve teardown. Count
+changes within a prepared capacity reuse the compiled callables, including
+reduction. Static internal kernel recipes remain available for comparison.
+
+MLA 2CTA runtime plans size scratch from the prepared policy bound, replacing
+the former implicit128-split reservation. Parallel reduction eligibility is
+retained for runtime counts and selected from the capacity/topology envelope.
+Dense FMHA runtime plans use staged page-ID loads because reducing the split
+count can grow a CTA's span beyond a held window qualified for a static count.
